keting campaign on physicians' knowledge and practices.</article-title><source>Genet Med</source><volume>8</volume><fpage>361</fpage><lpage>370</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16778598</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pmed.1000138-Suther1"><label>7</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Suther</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Goodson</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Barriers to the provision of genetic services by primary care physicians: A systematic review of the literature.</article-title><source>Genet Med</source><volume>5</volume><fpage>70</fpage><lpage>76</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12644775</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pmed.1000138-Watson1"><label>8</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Watson</surname><given-names>EK</given-names></name><name><surname>Shickle</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Qureshi</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Emery</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Austoker</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>The 'new genetics' and primary care: GPs' views on their role and their educational needs.</article-title><source>Fam Pract</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>420</fpage><lpage>425</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10493715</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pmed.1000138-Korf1"><label>9</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Korf</surname><given-names>BR</given-names></name><name><surname>Feldman</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Wiesner</surname><given-names>GL</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Report of Banbury Summit meeting on training of physicia